    "\n",
    "The raw time series allows us to observe the overall movement in automobile sales across the quarters. However, short-term fluctuations can make it difficult to identify the underlying pattern.\n",
    "\n",
    "**Simple Moving Averages**\n",
    "\n",
    "A $k$-period simple moving average at period $t$ is calculated as:\n",
    "\n",
    "$$\n",
    "\\text{MA}_t =\n",
    "\\frac{1}{k}\n",
    "\\sum_{i=0}^{k-1}Y_{t-i}\n",
    "$$\n",
    "\n",
    "For this example, we calculate two moving averages:\n",
    "\n",
    "- **3-period moving average:** places greater emphasis on recent movements and therefore responds relatively quickly to changes in sales.\n",
    "- **10-period moving average:** produces greater smoothing and is less sensitive to short-term fluctuations.\n",
    "\n",
    ":::{.callout-tip title=\"📊 Moving Average Analysis\"}"
   ]
